{"name":"Indulgence","hex":"#533d47","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"indulgence","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of indulging.","Tolerance."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To provide with an indulgence."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/indulgence"}],"entries":[{"title":"Indulgence","blocks":[{"text":"In the teaching of the Catholic Church, an indulgence is \"a way to reduce the amount of punishment one has to undergo for (forgiven) sins\". The Catechism of the Catholic Church describes an indulgence as \"a remission before God of the temporal punishment due to sins whose guilt has already been forgiven, which the faithful Christian who is duly disposed gains under certain prescribed conditions…\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Apostolic_Blessing_and_Plenary_Indulgence_Parchment_-_1948_Oct_26%2C_Pope_Pius_XII_to_Della_Mora_Antonietta_%28DSC_2566%29.jpg/330px-Apostolic_Blessing_and_Plenary_Indulgence_Parchment_-_1948_Oct_26%2C_Pope_Pius_XII_to_Della_Mora_Antonietta_%28DSC_2566%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indulgence","wikidata":"Q44777"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Indulgence_San_Giovanni_in_Laterano_2006-09-07.jpg/500px-Indulgence_San_Giovanni_in_Laterano_2006-09-07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Indulgence_San_Giovanni_in_Laterano_2006-09-07.jpg/1280px-Indulgence_San_Giovanni_in_Laterano_2006-09-07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Indulgence_San_Giovanni_in_Laterano_2006-09-07.jpg/500px-Indulgence_San_Giovanni_in_Laterano_2006-09-07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Inscripti